<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<PLUGIN name="UGREEN-DXP4800Pro-LEDs" author="EllipticSet" pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/EllipticSet/UGREEN-DXP4800Pro-LEDs/main/UGREEN-DXP4800Pro-LEDs.plg" support="https://github.com/EllipticSet/UGREEN-DXP4800Pro-LEDs/issues" version="1.2.0" icon="icons/icon-azure.png" launch="Settings/LED-Settings" min="7.3.2">
  <CHANGES>
###1.2.0
- Put tab descriptions below the NAS image and add click-to-open help to every setting.
- Replace save/error notices with dismissible, theme-aware feedback.
- Add percentage brightness in 10% steps, defaulting to 70%, with a raw-value display option and 0% off.
- Move connectivity checks and their interval to Advanced Settings.
- Restart standby breathing together when the set of sleeping drives changes.

###1.1.5
- Use /LED-Settings with the name LED Settings and show the installed version inside the tab bar.
- Enable the standard ATA mapping 1 2 3 4; empty bays remain off and added drives are detected automatically.
- Migrate previous occupancy-based defaults while retaining manually reordered ports.
- Move ATA mapping and the optional diagnostic guide to Advanced Settings and remove its NAS image.
- Remove mandatory first-time detection and installation mapping verbosity.
- Update documentation and installer, monitor, UI and package regression checks.

###1.1.0
- Replace the Settings and Plugins icons with LED indicators and adjustment sliders, with coordinated variants for all four Unraid themes.
- Rename the Unraid Settings entry to "LED Settings"; keep the plugin name "UGREEN DXP4800 Pro LEDs".
- Recreate the README icon animation with the new design and rounded, transparent corners.

###1.0.3
- Remove unused upstream packaging and tools; retain dependency sources, licences and provenance.
- Verify the committed offline package before rebuilding and normalize archive metadata.
- Check settings recovery and monitor restart failures explicitly.
- Clarify LED behaviour, refresh intervals, brightness and validation documentation.

###1.0.2
- Follow the active Unraid theme for plugin and Settings icons, including live Theme Switch changes.

###1.0.1
- Fix the plugin manager icon path and replace the remaining lightbulb page tag.
- Reinstall packaged files and reject stale WebGUI assets before reporting success.

###1.0.0
- Introduce NAS outline icons for all four Unraid themes.
- Highlight Settings &gt; LED Settings after installation.
- Adopt semantic versioning (major.minor.patch).

###2026.10.03.6
- Restore UGREEN DXP4800 Pro LEDs as the public plugin name; retain LED Settings for the Unraid Settings page.

###2026.10.03.5
- Add Done and Show guide controls to collapse and reopen the drive setup guide; remember dismissal in this browser.
- Remove the duplicate drive mapping note below the controls.
- Refresh README screenshots and show smaller clickable previews.

###2026.10.03.4
- Remove LED highlights from Advanced Settings.
- Add prominent first-time drive LED mapping instructions, the detection command and a README guide link.

###2026.10.03.3
- Rename the interface to LED Settings; add native Power, LAN, Drives and Advanced tabs with front-panel LED highlights.
- Apply and restore defaults per tab while preserving other settings.
- Remove the Beta label from plugin descriptions and Community Applications metadata.
- Add desktop and mobile interface screenshots to the README.

###2026.10.03.2
- Allow Unraid 7.3 and later when the exact packaged kernel matches; retain the kernel guard.

###2026.10.03.1
- Refresh documentation and README badges; update plugin descriptions.

###2026.10.02.4
- Remove the manually loaded LED module with rmmod; report unload failures.

###2026.10.02.3
- Public GitHub and Community Applications metadata; preserve settings on updates with rollback.
- English plugin listing and documentation; compact title and description.
- Keep the native Unraid CSRF fix.
- DXP4800 Pro build: Intel legacy I801, isolated workers, native settings, offline installer.
</CHANGES>
  <FILE Run="/bin/bash">
    <INLINE>set -euo pipefail
scratch=$(mktemp -d /tmp/ugreen-pro-install.XXXXXX)
trap 'rm -rf -- "$scratch"' EXIT
base64 -d &gt; "$scratch/bundle.tar.xz" &lt;&lt;'UGREEN_PAYLOAD'
